Krita Nova 22 - multi-threaded "close gap" for the Fill tool

A contiguous fill runs as one job on one CPU core (only "Fill similar
regions" is split into parallel jobs). With "Close gap" on, most of the time
goes into KisGapMap's gap distance search: for every opaque (line art) pixel
near the fill it searches a half circle of radius "gap size" in four octants.
That was computed lazily, tile by tile (64x64 px), as the scanline fill
reached each tile.

KisGapMap::lazyDistance() now computes the whole 3x3 tile neighborhood of a
requested tile at once, the tiles in parallel on up to 8 threads (a fill
that reaches a tile almost always continues into its neighbors). The per-tile
state (accessor, tile position, tile data pointer) moved into a
DistanceContext, one per thread; a tile computation writes distances only
inside its own tile and only reads opacity, which is loaded (for 5x5 tiles)
before the parallel part. TILE_DISTANCE_LOADED is set after all threads are
done. Results are identical; the flood fill itself (KisScanlineFill) stays
sequential.

